Fix accent: add padding-top to .logo .l1 and .logo .l2 with negative margin, or simply add `padding-top:.14em; margin-top:-.14em;` to each. Since background-clip:text paints background only within element box including padding. Let's do that. But padding affects flex baseline? align-items:baseline. Negative margin-top offsets layout. Actually padding-top increases height and pushes text down; negative margin-top pulls element up. Baseline alignment may be affected. Better: use `background-origin: border-box; background-size: 100% 120%;`? Background-clip:text clips to text glyphs but background is still painted only within background positioning area (padding box). The glyph accent lies outside the padding box at top, so no paint. Adding `padding-top:.14em;margin-top:-.14em` will expand painting area upward while keeping visual position (padding pushes content down .14em; negative margin moves box up .14em, net same text position). For flex baseline, margin-top doesn't affect baseline of text? It shifts box. Should be fine. Also add display:inline-block maybe not needed since spans are flex items.

Let's apply. Also lighten ground and lighting.

Key improvements:
1. Title logo accent.
2. Game brightness: 
   - Ground base from #0b100d to #141a15? Night scene should still be dark but visible. Increase ground palette significantly.
   - Ambient overlay .76 → .62, ambient radius bigger 280, gradient stronger.
   - Flashlight cone: destination-out alpha currently max .3 at center (remove only 30% of darkness) which is why cone barely visible. Should be much stronger: 0.85 center, 0.7 mid, 0.4 edge. Since destination-out alpha accumulates across 5 layers! Actually drawing 5 nested cones each with alpha .3 will accumulate to ~0.83 near center. Hmm, 1-(0.7^5)=0.83. But near the outer spread only the largest cone covers, so edge is .3. Center removed 83% → leaves 17% of 76% = 13% dark. Not much light. Better: single cone with gradient along radius? A radial gradient from player at 0 to dist, with alpha high at center and fading to 0 at end, but clipped to cone shape. Use clip path then fill radial gradient with destination-out: center alpha .95 → outer .15. Plus 3 layered for soft edges. Let's implement:

```
