Also roof border #2a333a → #38444d, equipment colors. Not critical.

Now render.js lighting. Replace drawLighting ambient and flashlight sections and add warm cone.

Current ambient:
```
lctx.fillStyle = 'rgba(3,6,12,.76)';
...
ambR = 235*zoom; gradient 0 .95, .55 .52, 1 0
```
Change overlay to .68 maybe. Ambient radius 300*zoom, center 0.98, .5 .6, 1 0.

Flashlight: replace loop with clipped gradient cones.

Warm cone after drawImage and before lamps? Add after lamp/fire glow maybe. We'll add just before aura.

Implementation:

```
  // linterna: haz principal
  const dist = 680 * zoom;
  const beam = (spread, strength) => {
    lctx.save();
    lctx.beginPath();
    lctx.moveTo(px, py);
    lctx.arc(px, py, dist, player.angle - spread, player.angle + spread);
    lctx.closePath();
    lctx.clip();
    const cg = lctx.createRadialGradient(px, py, 16, px, py, dist);
    cg.addColorStop(0, `rgba(0,0,0,${strength})`);
    cg.addColorStop(0.22, `rgba(0,0,0,${strength * 0.9})`);
    cg.addColorStop(0.6, `rgba(0,0,0,${strength * 0.55})`);
    cg.addColorStop(0.88, `rgba(0,0,0,${strength * 0.18})`);
    cg.addColorStop(1, 'rgba(0,0,0,0)');
    lctx.fillStyle = cg;
    lctx.fillRect(px - dist, py - dist, dist * 2, dist * 2);
    lctx.restore();
  };
  beam(0.6, 0.55);
  beam(0.34, 0.85);
```

Note destination-out with fillRect using radial gradient works.

Then additive warm cone in ctx:
```
  const beamGlow = (spread, alpha) => {
    ctx.save();
    ctx.beginPath(); moveTo... arc... clip();
    const bg = ctx.createRadialGradient(px,py,0,px,py,dist*0.95);
    bg.addColorStop(0,`rgba(255,196,120,${alpha})`);
    bg.addColorStop(.4,`rgba(255,170,80,${alpha*.55})`);
    bg.addColorStop(1,'rgba(255,140,40,0)');
    ctx.fillStyle=bg; ctx.fillRect(...);
    ctx.restore();
  };
```
Since ctx is already globalCompositeOperation 'lighter' inside the save block, calling ctx.save then clip fine. Use after aura.

Also ambient in-game ground is drawn then dark overlay. Let's increase darkness overlay .68.

