I made a syntax error: `body.touch .buff{bottom:calc(240px + var(--safe-b))}` missing `;` before `}`? It's `bottom:calc(240px + var(--safe-b))` then `}` — CSS allows missing semicolon before closing brace, but `var(--safe-b))` has two closing parens? Let's check: `calc(240px + var(--safe-b))` = calc( ... var(--safe-b) ) → correct one closing for var, one for calc: `var(--safe-b))` yes two. Then `}` closes rule. Missing semicolon is valid. But I wrote `...safe-b))}` which is fine.

Wait the original base body.touch .buff had bottom 96; I changed to 240. But the line I wrote is `body.touch .buff{bottom:calc(240px + var(--safe-b))}` — no semicolon before `}`. Valid CSS. Let's verify with a quick parse via browser later.

But also I need to check that the media query for min-width 721 comes before base body.touch rules. In CSS, base rules after media query override media query at all widths! Yes: order matters. The base body.touch .weapon-panel at line 562 comes after @media min-width 721, so on tablets it will override the media query's bottom:16 with bottom:168. That's not what we want. Originally the base had bottom:16 and media query had bottom:16, no issue. Now base bottom 168 overrides tablet. Need to put base before media query, or add tablet override after base. Simpler: change the min-width media query to appear after the base rules, or add bottom:16 inside a new @media after base. Let's restructure order: move the @media (min-width:721px) block after base body.touch rules. The current order:

```
@media (min-width:721px){...}
body.touch .weapon-panel{...168...}
...
```

So on tablet, base 168 wins. We want tablet 16. Add another @media (min-width:721px) after base:

```
@media (min-width:721px){
  body.touch .weapon-panel{bottom:calc(16px + var(--safe-b))}
  body.touch .buff{bottom:calc(100px + var(--safe-b))}
  body.touch #toast{top:calc(120px + var(--safe-t))}
}
```

